Scene: GroomSimulatedCoat
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Groom guide simulation and body collision -- the moving path's live scene
# (#1250).
#
# A NEW scene rather than a change to Scenes/GroomBoundCoat.olo, for the reason
# that scene's own header gives about ITS neighbours: #1249's bound-coat scene
# is the baseline every binding capture was measured against, and adding a
# solver to it would invalidate them.
#
# WHAT IS DIFFERENT FROM GroomBoundCoat.olo: BristleCoat carries a
# GroomSimulationComponent. Nothing else changed.
#
# HOW TO SEE THE FEATURE, in one step: press Play and rotate BristleBody. The
# coat swings, settles and holds itself off the body instead of following it
# rigidly. Toggle GroomSimulationComponent -> Enabled off with the body still
# moving and the coat snaps back to the rigid #1249 behaviour -- that pair IS
# the feature, and it is the A/B every capture in the PR uses.
#
# IT DOES NOT MOVE IN EDIT MODE, and that is deliberate rather than broken: a
# scene must not change just from being open, so the solver's clock is zero
# outside Play. Pressing Play is what starts it; pausing holds the pose.
#
# THE COAT IS AUTHORED SOFT HERE -- Stiffness 18 rather than the 90 default --
# because the point of this scene is to SHOW the motion. A production pelt holds
# its groom and only trembles, which is correct and invisible in a screenshot.
#
# The body collision proxy is FITTED from BristleBody's own vertices, one
# capsule per bone; there is no rig to place. ColliderRadiusScale is the lever.
# Set DebugView to 3 to draw both the guides and the fitted capsules (the
# editor's Component Gizmos toggle gates them, so a capture turns them off).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
